{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ConformalGuard: multi-agent trace experiment, rerun (Kaggle)\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook runs only the multi-agent experiment: it generates sessions with the corrected simulator and trains and evaluates the scorers. The R-Judge experiments of the earlier notebook are finished and are not repeated.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What changed since the first run**\n",
    "\n",
    "- The Claude requests no longer contain a free-text field before the action, which the provider declined as `reasoning_extraction`. The generator now probes request configurations on three throw-away sessions and uses the first one the provider accepts; if none is accepted for `MAS_CLAUDE_MODEL`, it uses `MAS_CLAUDE_BACKUP`.\n",
    "- An agent that uses up its tool calls now gets a turn to report. In the first run most researchers were cut off and their findings lost.\n",
    "- Sessions of the first run are not reused: they came from the old simulator.\n",
    "\n",
    "**How to run it**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Trial (about 10 minutes, no GPU).** Accelerator **None**, Internet **on**, `TRIAL = True`, **Run All**. Then read three things in the output of the generation cell: the `probe:` lines (which configuration was accepted), the `usage:` line (refused steps should be 0 or close), and the printed session (the researcher should report its findings and the acting agent should send, post, upload or share something). The cell after it prints a cost estimate for the full run from the measured token counts.\n",
    "2. **Full run.** `TRIAL = False`, Accelerator **GPU T4 x2** if you have about 3 hours of quota left (otherwise leave it on None and set `MAS_SPLITS = 20`; training on CPU takes several hours), then **Save Version \u2192 Save & Run All (Commit)**. Download `mas_rerun_results.zip` from the saved version's Output tab.\n",
    "\n",
    "Secrets: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (and `OPENAI_API_KEY` if you set `MAS_OPENAI_MODEL`), attached to this notebook. Never paste a key into a cell."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "TRIAL = True                 # True: 10-minute check. False: the full run (use Save & Run All).\n",
    "DEADLINE_HOURS = 8.0         # the full run stops waiting for generation after this many hours\n",
    "\n",
    "MAS_CLAUDE_MODEL = \"claude-opus-5-5\"\n",
    "MAS_CLAUDE_BACKUP = \"claude-opus-4-8\"   # used only if the provider declines MAS_CLAUDE_MODEL's requests; \"\" for none\n",
    "MAS_CLAUDE_EFFORT = \"low\"\n",
    "MAS_CLAUDE_SESSIONS = 600\n",
    "\n",
    "MAS_OPENAI_MODEL = \"\"        # e.g. \"gpt-6-astra\"; \"\" skips OpenAI. A small set is enough: it is used for the cross-model test.\n",
    "MAS_OPENAI_SESSIONS = 80\n",
    "\n",
    "MAS_SPLITS = 50\n",
    "MAS_WORKERS = 8\n",
    "\n",
    "# USD per million tokens, for the cost estimate only. Check the providers' pricing pages and edit.\n",
    "CLAUDE_PRICES = dict(inp=4.0, out=20.0, cache_read=0.20, cache_write=5.0)\n",
    "OPENAI_PRICES = dict(inp=10.0, out=50.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "import os, signal, subprocess, time\n",
    "T0 = time.time()\n",
    "os.makedirs(\"/kaggle/temp\", exist_ok=True)\n",
    "os.chdir(\"/kaggle/temp\")\n",
    "os.environ[\"PYTHONUNBUFFERED\"] = \"1\"\n",
    "FAILED = []\n",
    "def sh(cmd):\n",
    "    print(\"$\", cmd, flush=True)\n",
    "    get_ipython().system(cmd)\n",
    "    code = get_ipython().user_ns.get(\"_exit_code\", 0)\n",
    "    if code:\n",
    "        FAILED.append(cmd)\n",
    "        print(f\"!! exit code {code}: this command failed; later stages still run\", flush=True)\n",
    "    return code\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(\"/kaggle/temp/CV\"):\n",
    "    sh(\"git clone -q --depth 1 -b claude/implement-conformalguard-UGndd https://example.org/anonymous")\n",
    "    sh(\"pip -q install sentence-transformers scikit-learn pytest anthropic openai\")\n",
    "os.chdir(\"/kaggle/temp/CV/ConformalGuard\")\n",
    "sh(\"git log --oneline -1\")\n",
    "RUNS = \"runs_trial\" if TRIAL else \"runs\"\n",
    "ZIP = \"/kaggle/working/\" + (\"mas_rerun_TRIAL.zip\" if TRIAL else \"mas_rerun_results.zip\")\n",
    "os.makedirs(f\"{RUNS}/logs\", exist_ok=True)\n",
    "def pack():\n",
    "    sh(f\"cd /kaggle/temp/CV/ConformalGuard && zip -qr {ZIP} {RUNS} -x '*/cache/*' && ls -la {ZIP}\")\n",
    "def hours():\n",
    "    return (time.time() - T0) / 3600"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# API keys come from Kaggle Secrets and are only placed in this process's environment.\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    from kaggle_secrets import UserSecretsClient\n",
    "    _secrets = UserSecretsClient()\n",
    "    for _k in (\"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\", \"OPENAI_API_KEY\"):\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            os.environ[_k] = _secrets.get_secret(_k)\n",
    "            print(_k, \"loaded\")\n",
    "        except Exception:\n",
    "            print(_k, \"not set\")\n",
    "except ImportError:\n",
    "    print(\"not on Kaggle: using keys already in the environment, if any\")\n",
    "HAVE_CLAUDE = bool(os.environ.get(\"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\")) and bool(MAS_CLAUDE_MODEL)\n",
    "HAVE_OPENAI = bool(os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\")) and bool(MAS_OPENAI_MODEL)\n",
    "print(\"Claude agents:\", \"on\" if HAVE_CLAUDE else \"off\", \"| OpenAI agents:\", \"on\" if HAVE_OPENAI else \"off\")\n",
    "sh(\"python -m pytest tests/test_mas.py -q\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Generate sessions\n",
    "\n",
    "In the trial: 4 sessions per agent model, in the foreground. In the full run: both providers in the background, each with a second pass that retries failed sessions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "N_CLAUDE = 4 if TRIAL else MAS_CLAUDE_SESSIONS\n",
    "N_OPENAI = 4 if TRIAL else MAS_OPENAI_SESSIONS\n",
    "PASSES = 1 if TRIAL else 2\n",
    "backup = f\"--backup-model {MAS_CLAUDE_BACKUP} \" if MAS_CLAUDE_BACKUP else \"\"\n",
    "CHAINS = {}\n",
    "if HAVE_CLAUDE:\n",
    "    CHAINS[\"claude\"] = [f\"python scripts/mas_generate_claude.py --model {MAS_CLAUDE_MODEL} {backup}--effort {MAS_CLAUDE_EFFORT} \"\n",
    "                        f\"--n {N_CLAUDE} --seed-start 0 --workers {MAS_WORKERS} --out {RUNS}/mas_claude\"] * PASSES\n",
    "if HAVE_OPENAI:\n",
    "    CHAINS[\"openai\"] = [f\"python scripts/mas_generate_openai.py --model {MAS_OPENAI_MODEL} --n {N_OPENAI} \"\n",
    "                        f\"--seed-start 100000 --workers {MAS_WORKERS} --out {RUNS}/mas_openai\"] * PASSES\n",
    "JOBS = {}\n",
    "for name, cmds in CHAINS.items():\n",
    "    if TRIAL:\n",
    "        for c in cmds:\n",
    "            sh(c)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        log = open(f\"{RUNS}/logs/{name}.log\", \"w\")\n",
    "        JOBS[name] = subprocess.Popen([\"bash\", \"-c\", \" ; \".join(cmds)], stdout=log, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,\n",
    "                                      start_new_session=True)\n",
    "        print(f\"started the {name} generation in the background; log: {RUNS}/logs/{name}.log\")\n",
    "while any(p.poll() is None for p in JOBS.values()) and hours() < DEADLINE_HOURS:\n",
    "    time.sleep(120)\n",
    "    for name in JOBS:\n",
    "        sh(f\"echo '[{hours():.1f} h] {name}:' $(tail -n 1 {RUNS}/logs/{name}.log)\")\n",
    "for name, p in JOBS.items():\n",
    "    if p.poll() is None:\n",
    "        os.killpg(p.pid, signal.SIGTERM)\n",
    "        print(f\"{name} generation stopped at the deadline; the sessions written so far are kept\")\n",
    "    print(f\"--- {name} log\"); sh(f\"cat {RUNS}/logs/{name}.log | grep -v 'sessions written'\")\n",
    "FILES = [f for f in (f\"{RUNS}/mas_claude/sessions.jsonl\", f\"{RUNS}/mas_openai/sessions.jsonl\") if os.path.exists(f)]\n",
    "pack()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Look at what was generated\n",
    "\n",
    "Read the printed session. In the trial this is the check that decides whether to start the full run: the researcher should report what it found, and the acting agent should act on it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "for f in FILES:\n",
    "    sh(f\"python scripts/mas_show.py {f}\" + (\" --session 0\" if TRIAL else \"\"))\n",
    "if TRIAL:\n",
    "    print(\"\\nCost estimate for the full run, from the token counts measured above (prices are the ones set in the first cell):\")\n",
    "    if os.path.exists(f\"{RUNS}/mas_claude/sessions.jsonl\"):\n",
    "        p = CLAUDE_PRICES\n",
    "        sh(f\"python scripts/mas_cost.py {RUNS}/mas_claude/sessions.jsonl --n {MAS_CLAUDE_SESSIONS} --in-price {p['inp']} \"\n",
    "           f\"--out-price {p['out']} --cache-read-price {p['cache_read']} --cache-write-price {p['cache_write']}\")\n",
    "    if os.path.exists(f\"{RUNS}/mas_openai/sessions.jsonl\"):\n",
    "        p = OPENAI_PRICES\n",
    "        sh(f\"python scripts/mas_cost.py {RUNS}/mas_openai/sessions.jsonl --n {MAS_OPENAI_SESSIONS} --in-price {p['inp']} --out-price {p['out']}\")\n",
    "    print(\"If the estimate is above what you want to spend, lower MAS_CLAUDE_SESSIONS / MAS_OPENAI_SESSIONS before the full run.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Train and evaluate\n",
    "\n",
    "Random splits over all sessions, and, if two agent models are present, training on one model's sessions and testing on the other's. Skipped in the trial: four sessions per model are too few to train on."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if TRIAL:\n",
    "    print(\"Nothing to do in the trial.\")\n",
    "elif FILES:\n",
    "    sh(f\"python scripts/mas_run.py --sessions {' '.join(FILES)} --features st --reps {MAS_SPLITS} --out {RUNS}/mas_exp\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"no sessions were generated: see the logs above\")\n",
    "pack()\n",
    "if FAILED:\n",
    "    print(f\"{len(FAILED)} command(s) FAILED; scroll up to their output:\")\n",
    "    for c in FAILED:\n",
    "        print(\"  \", c)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"every command exited normally\")\n",
    "print(f\"finished after {hours():.2f} h. \" + (\"This was a TRIAL: check the probe lines, the refused-step count and the printed session, then set TRIAL = False.\"\n",
    "                                             if TRIAL else \"Download mas_rerun_results.zip from this version's Output tab.\"))"
   ]
  }
 ],
